---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';

import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const treatments = await getCollection('treatments');

const stats = [
  { number: `${treatments.length}`, label: 'Treatments offered' },
  { number: '4',    label: 'Service families' },
  { number: '100%', label: 'Disposable tools' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Our Story | Aura Blush Studio"
  description="How a permanent-makeup studio in Varanasi became a skin and laser studio too — and the standards that had to come with it."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <span class="page-header__eyebrow">About Us</span>
    <h1>The Aura Blush Story</h1>
    <div class="page-header__rule"></div>
    <p class="page-header__lede">
      How a permanent-makeup studio in Varanasi became a skin and laser studio too — and the
      standards that had to come with it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-image">
          <img src="/images/studio.jpg" alt="Inside Aura Blush Studio" loading="lazy" />
        </div>

        <div class="about-content">
          <SectionHeading title="From pigment to skin" subtitle="Our Philosophy" alignment="left" />
          <p>
            Aura Blush was founded in Sigra to close a gap this city had: high-end cosmetic
            work you did not have to travel to Delhi or Lucknow for. Permanent makeup shouldn't
            look like a tattoo — it should look like makeup applied by someone who knows your
            face, that simply never washes off.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our philosophy is rooted in <strong>subtle enhancement</strong>. We don't work from
            one-size-fits-all stencils. Every set of brows and lips is custom-mapped to your
            bone structure and your natural asymmetry — because faces aren't symmetrical, and
            results that pretend otherwise are the ones that look done.
          </p>
          <p>
            The menu grew because our clients kept asking the same follow-up question. Brows
            and lips solve one thing; they don't touch texture, tone or the pigmentation that
            was bothering someone long before they booked. So the menu grew into four families
            of treatment — <strong>and the screening that has to come with them</strong>.
            Patch tests before laser. Dermatology clearance before any mole. Topicals and
            peels before we will point a device at melasma.
          </p>

          <div class="stats-grid">
            {stats.map(stat => (
              <div class="stat">
                <span class="number">{stat.number}</span>
                <span class="label">{stat.label}</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-offset">
    <div class="container values">
      <SectionHeading title="What we won't compromise on" subtitle="Standards" />
      <ul class="accent-list values-list">
        <li><strong>Sterility.</strong> Single-use needles, blades and laser tips, opened in front of you, autoclaved workstation, sharps disposal on site.</li>
        <li><strong>Honesty.</strong> If your skin, medication or expectations make a treatment a bad idea, we say so and don't take the booking.</li>
        <li><strong>Scope.</strong> One artist working strictly inside what she is certified for. Anything that needs a doctor is referred to one — we don't improvise near a diagnosis.</li>
        <li><strong>Evidence over speed.</strong> The faster option is often the one that causes rebound pigmentation. We treat in the order the literature supports, even when it costs us the sale.</li>
        <li><strong>Patience.</strong> Mapping takes as long as it takes, and a collagen course takes the months it takes. Nothing here is sold as a single-visit fix that isn't one.</li>
        <li><strong>Honest naming.</strong> We do not sell fairness, whitening or lightening, whatever it is called this year. Even tone is a real result; a different complexion is not one we would offer you.</li>
        <li><strong>Aftercare.</strong> Every client leaves with written instructions, sunscreen that suits this climate, and a WhatsApp line for the days that matter most.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 3.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 5rem;
    }
  }

  .about-image {
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }

  .about-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: clamp(320px, 45vw, 520px);
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .about-content p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .about-content strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .stats-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }

  .stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .number {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .values {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .values-list li {
    padding-bottom: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .values-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .values-list strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
